WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.792
By the end of this module, you should be able to recognize long and wide data, explain the grain of each structure,

00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:10.242
and move between the two forms.

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:18.502
You will learn how to create pivot style results with conditional aggregation, how to un pivot wide columns back into

00:00:18.502 --> 00:00:23.412
rows, and how to preserve the difference between a missing value and a true zero.

00:00:23.412 --> 00:00:28.912
You will also learn how joins and aggregation can change the meaning of a reshape.

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:35.442
Most importantly, you should be able to explain why a particular output shape is appropriate for the next analytical

00:00:35.442 --> 00:00:36.728
task.
